// CHECKOUT PROMENADE — STEEL STRING STROLL — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CHECKOUT PROMENADE as a sunny bossa-pop on a steel-string guitar — a game alternate of
// shop, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces
// the live song. The second remix, after BROWSING BOSSA.
// 
// Peter: "One with steel string guitar. Maybe a light tight kit rather than brushes
// (with a small tight snare)."
// 
// The tune is the shop's, note for note (shop.js lead, bars 7–14), with its own harmony
// line and twinkle, and the bossa remix's chords, one every half bar:
//   A  | C6/9  Am11 | Dm9  G13 |      (twice)
//   B  | Fmaj9 Em7 | Am7  Dm9 G13 |   (twice; G13 on beat four, the shop's turnaround)
// voiced as open steel-string shapes. 112 BPM, swing 56. The steel-string strums straight
// eighths (D . U D U D U) with an alternate strum, up-strokes 4 dB under on the top four
// strings; a 12-string picks the shapes on top. The bass strolls: the root, then a scale
// step into the next root. A small dry kit: a round kick, a little rim-heavy snare on two
// and four with its own ghosts, tight closed hats, a sidestick backbeat in the quiet
// bars; tambourine and shaker only in the return.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the 12-string alone; the steel strum, bass, hats, sidestick and
//          celesta at bar 3
//   5–8    A — VIBES have the tune, an octave up; the kit in
//   9–12   B — PIANO has the tune; the marimba under it on the shop's harmony line;
//          organ pad, 12-string
//   13–16  A — vibes, the marimba on the harmony line, the celesta twinkle
//   17–20  B — piano and vibes an octave apart; organ, 12-string
//   21–28  BRIDGE, half time — the STEEL GUITAR has the tune at half speed, a chord a
//          bar; the marimba on the harmony line under it; organ; the vibes climb back
//   29–40  RETURN, fuller — A B A: vibes over piano, marimba harmony, organ, 12-string
//          rolling, celesta; tambourine, shaker, ghost snares, an open-hat lift
//   41–44  wind-down — the piano on B, the marimba under it, sidestick and hats
//   45–48  the steel strum and the vibes on the A phrase, the pickup back into bar 5
// 
// Mix: master gain −1 (the bossa's −4 read −24 LUFS), high shelves on the vibes, piano
// and guitars, a low shelf on the bass. The loop is bars 5–48. Unrendered and
// unlevelled: lane gains are set by reasoning.
// 48 bars at 112, 103 s. Written by work/local/_shop-remix-steel.mjs
// through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
